WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:05.820
Did you know that once, a part of Kale's&nbsp;
questline had you looking around for a bird,

00:00:05.820 --> 00:00:11.040
with a letter strapped to its leg?
Have you seen a crow around here by any chance?

00:00:11.040 --> 00:00:16.080
You know, a burial crow,&nbsp;
with a letter fastened to its claw?

00:00:16.080 --> 00:00:22.740
I'll give you a generous sum for it, of course.
And down here, we can find it. A

00:00:22.740 --> 00:00:26.280
so-called "Burial Crow".
And if you kill it, you can

00:00:26.280 --> 00:00:30.240
loot the "Burial Crow's Letter".
Which progresses Kale's questline,

00:00:30.240 --> 00:00:35.880
helping him to locate the underground area&nbsp;
where his brothers were entombed, long ago.

00:00:35.880 --> 00:00:41.400
This event in particular is a restoration of&nbsp;
Kale's cut questline, and if you'd like to see

00:00:41.400 --> 00:00:45.300
the full thing, then Sekiro Dubi has a full&nbsp;
restoration of it, over on their channel.

00:00:45.900 --> 00:00:51.600
But it's not just the questline that might relate to the burial crows:you know those notes that&nbsp;
you usually buy from merchants,

00:00:51.600 --> 00:00:56.220
that give you hints about the world?&nbsp;
Well according to some version 1.0 text,

00:00:56.220 --> 00:01:00.180
it's also possible that hunting&nbsp;
burial crows was originally the

00:01:00.180 --> 00:01:01.474
method by which you were supposed to loot these notes.

00:01:04.860 --> 00:01:09.000
And while we're speaking about the merchants, did you know that at one point,&nbsp;
there was planned to be a travelling merchant

00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:15.840
who actually wandered around the map in Limgrave?
According to Sekiro Dubi, evidence that merchants

00:01:15.840 --> 00:01:20.280
actually traveled survives in the&nbsp;
unused "walkroutes" that are found

00:01:20.280 --> 00:01:25.620
in a couple of Elden Ring's maps.
For example, this is NPC 802,

00:01:25.620 --> 00:01:31.020
who could be found here on the western coast..
before setting up camp here, by the bridge of

00:01:31.020 --> 00:01:34.740
sacrifice south of the evergaol...
Then here in the mistwood...

00:01:34.740 --> 00:01:38.640
and finally at Stormhill,&nbsp;
near the Saint's bridge.

00:01:38.640 --> 00:01:45.360
To be clear, NPC 802 is an earlier type of&nbsp;
merchant - one that actually had much deeper lore,

00:01:45.360 --> 00:01:51.420
at the time. As the story goes, this merchant is&nbsp;
actually aware of the dungeon underneath Leyndell

00:01:51.420 --> 00:01:59.220
where his brothers are entombed, and wanders&nbsp;
around out of fear. Fear of staying in the

00:01:59.220 --> 00:02:05.280
same place, and being locked up like his kin.
It's great storytelling, and it's a shame it

00:02:12.793 --> 00:02:16.320
So one of the best strategies for taking out the

00:02:16.320 --> 00:02:21.060
Godskin Duo - is sleep. It takes one&nbsp;
godskin out of commission entirely,

00:02:21.060 --> 00:02:28.800
allowing the fight to become more of a 1 on 1.
But did you know that the Godskin are actually

00:02:28.800 --> 00:02:35.280
supposed to be able to wake eachother up? This&nbsp;
isn't even cut content. There's actually just

00:02:35.280 --> 00:02:39.600
a bug that prevents this interaction&nbsp;
from taking place, most of the time.

00:02:39.600 --> 00:02:44.040
As far as I can tell, this was first&nbsp;
noted by LilAggy, while they were

00:02:44.040 --> 00:02:50.160
doing a randomised race through Elden Ring.
And then in a comment thread begun by Ziostorm,

00:02:50.160 --> 00:02:55.440
everyone got to work uncovering the truth.
According to this twitter user, the Godskin

00:02:55.440 --> 00:03:01.020
boss is actually able to perform this scream&nbsp;
in the Windmill Village, if they're lured down

00:03:01.020 --> 00:03:06.360
the hill where a celebrant is asleep. 
So why doesn't it work in the Godskin arena?

00:03:06.360 --> 00:03:15.420
Well according to @thefifthmatt, the Godskin AI&nbsp;
is supposed to do this if a "friend" is asleep,

00:03:15.420 --> 00:03:21.300
but the friend detection is bugged out in&nbsp;
this arena because of the knights that patrol

00:03:21.300 --> 00:03:26.520
outside the arena. So if, and only if, you remove&nbsp;
every single knight patrolling around the arena,

00:03:26.520 --> 00:03:32.460
as well as the "hidden HP bar enemy",&nbsp;
it will work in their arena again.

00:03:32.460 --> 00:03:39.000
This might explain why the waking behaviour&nbsp;
works in boss randomisers. A lot of these end

00:03:39.000 --> 00:03:44.640
up with you fighting the Godskin duo outside&nbsp;
of their arena, so there aren't any patrolling

00:03:44.640 --> 00:03:54.120
enemies to bug out this intended effect.
As for a lore explanation..well, sleep and death

00:03:58.920 --> 00:04:07.680
do seem to overlap somewhat, as I discussed in my&nbsp;
Miquella lore video..so it makes some sense that

00:04:07.680 --> 00:04:13.800
the Godskins, being deeply aware of death, might&nbsp;
have developed away to wake eachother out of it.

00:04:16.980 --> 00:04:21.720
Speaking of death, did you know that some&nbsp;
of Those Who Live in Death..can do this?

00:04:25.140 --> 00:04:28.440
Some things are just better&nbsp;
without any explanation, you know?

00:04:29.460 --> 00:04:34.440
What also doesn't need any further explanation&nbsp;
at this point, is just how inspired From

00:04:34.440 --> 00:04:40.080
Software are by Kentaro Miura's berserk.
But just when you think you've seen every

00:04:40.080 --> 00:04:44.400
Berserk reference possible, another&nbsp;
reading reveals another reference.

00:04:44.400 --> 00:04:52.200
I was reading this panel, in chapter 82, when&nbsp;
I realised that Griffith's last tear is frozen

00:04:52.200 --> 00:04:59.460
- crystallised. Making it look identical to the&nbsp;
crystal tears that once fell from the Erdtree.

00:04:59.460 --> 00:05:03.960
Another consistent thing in a lot&nbsp;
of From's games is the presence

00:05:03.960 --> 00:05:11.700
of an enemy that should be hostile, but isn't.
And in Elden Ring, that phenomenon shows up here,

00:05:11.700 --> 00:05:17.640
towards the end of Leyndell capital, past&nbsp;
a set of misbegotten. A friendly dog,

00:05:17.640 --> 00:05:23.700
who won't attack you. No matter what you do.
Hopefully they never fix this in an update.

00:05:24.420 --> 00:05:29.700
One thing they HAVE finally fixed though, is&nbsp;
the Roar medallion. It used to be that this only

00:05:29.700 --> 00:05:36.180
buffed a few roar-effects, but now it properly&nbsp;
buffs a broad spectrum of attacks, including

00:05:36.180 --> 00:05:41.220
the roar-based dragon communion incantations..
Aspect of the Crucible: Breath..

00:05:41.220 --> 00:05:45.960
and even placidusax's Ruin.
Couple this with the highland axe,

00:05:45.960 --> 00:05:50.880
which also buffs roar attacks and can be&nbsp;
simply put in your offhand, and you'll be a

00:05:50.880 --> 00:05:56.280
force to be reckoned with. Good potential for&nbsp;
a roar build here somewhere now, I reckon.

00:05:56.280 --> 00:06:01.980
For number 8 - another thing that pops up in&nbsp;
almost every From Software game is the presence

00:06:01.980 --> 00:06:08.160
of a character named "Yuliya". In Demon's&nbsp;
Souls, it was Yuria the Witch. In Dark Souls,

00:06:08.160 --> 00:06:15.840
it was the undead merchant who muttered this name,&nbsp;
talking about his sword, or perhaps the famale

00:06:15.840 --> 00:06:26.760
undead merchant. Then Yulia was a character&nbsp;
in Dark Souls 3..then a major character in

00:06:27.420 --> 00:06:32.340
Deracine..and THEN she was even a character&nbsp;
in Elden Ring, before the name was changed.

00:06:32.340 --> 00:06:38.520
That's right. Go through the cut dialogue, and&nbsp;
you'll find lines spoken from an earlier time in

00:06:38.520 --> 00:06:45.840
development..back when a man named "Hoarah Loux&nbsp;
was the Gold Mask, and when Lady Yuliya was the

00:06:45.840 --> 00:06:52.980
name of the deathbed companion, who became Fia.
Speaking of Fia - there's something extremely

00:06:52.980 --> 00:06:58.680
curious going on here, at the northernmost&nbsp;
minor Erdtree upon the Altus Plateau.

00:06:58.680 --> 00:07:06.480
Here, an omen can be found, hunched over in&nbsp;
a circle with a set of commoners. But what's

00:07:06.480 --> 00:07:13.320
weird about them, is that these are all unique&nbsp;
character models. The omen has a black cape,

00:07:13.320 --> 00:07:17.040
and the commoners have a black set&nbsp;
with a shroud over their faces.

00:07:17.040 --> 00:07:23.160
And it's not just the models - they have unique&nbsp;
casting animations as well. The commoners and

00:07:23.160 --> 00:07:28.860
the omen are capable of casting Fia's Mist,&nbsp;
complete with the little smokey symbol of

00:07:28.860 --> 00:07:35.520
death that Fia's Mist specifically, conjures up.
I guess you could speculate that these enemies are

00:07:35.520 --> 00:07:43.740
agents of Fia, considering Fia's mist is a unique&nbsp;
deathblight incantation developed specifically by

00:07:43.740 --> 00:07:52.140
her..but at the very least, they're aligned&nbsp;
with Godwyn's deathblight, and the new age

00:07:52.140 --> 00:08:00.660
that his ending portends to. They're even&nbsp;
positioned right underneath a unique Minor

00:08:00.660 --> 00:08:08.220
Erdtree. One that's almost entirely dead. Which&nbsp;
reminds me of the Shadow of the Erdtree teaser,

00:08:08.220 --> 00:08:16.020
which might be showing Godwyn's Deathroot&nbsp;
clawing its way up and around the erdtree.

00:08:16.980 --> 00:08:21.160
I wonder if this little group&nbsp;
is related to that. Hmm.

00:08:21.840 --> 00:08:23.940
Anyway,
Speaking of

